HST Office: a recovery list that survives crashes and power cuts, the first copy after 30 seconds, and
documents closed without saving kept for 7 days.

- framework autorecovery.cxx: after every recovery copy and every save the configuration is written to
  disk synchronously (XFlushable, fsync'd by hst-profile-durability.patch) before the superseded copy is
  deleted; before, the entry still named the deleted copy for about a second ("Không thể phục hồi" after a
  crash in that window) and a power cut in the next seconds lost the entry. After every change of the
  RecoveryList, backup/hst-recovery-index.txt mirrors it (temporary file, fsync, rename).
- At start (AutoRecovery service, created before desktop's recovery check): index entries the
  configuration lost and orphaned recovery copies (<prefix>_<n>.od?, non-empty, younger than 7 days) come
  back into the RecoveryList, so the recovery dialog offers them; a copy replaces the missing or older copy
  of the only entry with the same name prefix, otherwise it becomes a new entry "<name> (recovery copy of
  <time>)". Unreferenced leftovers in backup/ older than 7 days (recovery copies, empty placeholders,
  lu*.tmp, .~lock.*#) are removed; *.bak and HST files are never touched.
- First recovery copy: a document without any copy (new, or just saved) is due 20 seconds after its first
  change; with upstream's 10-second wait for a pause in typing the copy lands about 30 seconds after the
  change (a document that reports itself modified while its dirty clock has not started yet, as during the
  first modify notification, counts as just changed). Then the normal interval; documents above the
  large-document size keep their own interval.
- "Tài liệu chưa lưu": a document closed while modified keeps its last recovery copy in user/hst-unsaved
  (<time>-<id>.<ext> + .txt description: title, original URL, module, times) instead of deleting it;
  the store is pruned to 7 days and 500 MB (oldest first) at every close and start. The bundled extension
  lists, opens and deletes them (org.hst.office.vi:UnsavedDocuments).
- Document tabs: emergency and session saves freeze hst-document-tabs.txt (no rewrite, no removal while
  the windows are hidden, none at the following quit); the file is written through a temporary file, fsync
  and rename, and right after a recovery has rebuilt the tabs.
- Reading the RecoveryList drops the per-session flags "handled" and "postponed": the early flush can
  store them while an AutoSave run is still going, and the recovery skipped such an entry as already done
  ("Chưa khôi phục" after a crash right after the first copy).
- desktop app.cxx: AutoRecovery starts before impl_checkRecoveryState so the restored entries count.
- framework strings + vi messages.po: titles of orphaned copies.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_recovery_durability_patches.py; tests/runtime/check-recovery-kill.py
(first copy, later copy, emergency save), tests/runtime/check-unsaved-documents.py.
